      "writtenOn": "2026-08-31T11:20:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is because the associations definition from PLDM PDR may not be applicable in bmcweb. \nFor example, a PDR could exposes the following structures:\n```\nNetwork Controller (Network Adapter / PCIeSwitch)\n|- ...\n|- Connector - Ethernet (Port)\n`- Connector - OSFP\n```\n\nGenerally, we will only creates D-Bus object for Network Controller and Port, and ignore the connector.\nHowever, if we strictly follows the structure here, we will be needing association for network controller \u003c-\u003e connector, and connector \u003c-\u003e port.",
      "parentUuid": "f04bf401_69b0bc15",
